# Shipped by the claude-code host component — do not edit by hand.
#
# Caps pytest-xdist's fan-out for every unit a user manager starts, `systemd-run --user`
# fan-out batches included. The package ships one copy to /usr/lib/environment.d, which every
# user manager reads at its start. None of those units read claude-rc.service's own
# PYTEST_XDIST_AUTO_NUM_WORKERS Environment= line; that reaches only the unit's cgroup.
#
# An ssh session does not read this file: pam_env reads /etc/environment and pam_env.conf, not
# environment.d. sshd-pytest-cap.conf.j2 carries the cap to ssh sessions.
#
# Same value as claude_code_rc_pytest_workers, not a separate number — raise them together,
# or the cap depends on how the session started (this role's CLAUDE.md has the third
# location, ~/.claude/settings.json's env block in the chezmoi repo).
#
# Takes effect when the user manager next starts; a running manager keeps what it started with.
PYTEST_XDIST_AUTO_NUM_WORKERS={{ claude_code_rc_pytest_workers }}
